WEBVTT

00:00:03.010 --> 00:00:04.370
Shugo, shugo!

00:00:04.370 --> 00:00:06.990
Start it off with a Doki! It's Shugo Chara time!

00:00:06.990 --> 00:00:09.770
Our story today is about a teacher!

00:00:09.770 --> 00:00:12.120
Teacher? You mean Nikaidou-sensei?

00:00:12.120 --> 00:00:15.730
That's right! Nikaidou-sensei, 
and Wakana-chan, too.

00:00:15.730 --> 00:00:18.060
Wakana-chan and Nikaidou-sensei?

00:00:18.060 --> 00:00:19.980
What could they possibly have in common?

00:00:19.980 --> 00:00:22.720
You'll have to stayed 
tuned to find out! {note: non-literal, but just as cliche}

00:00:22.720 --> 00:00:23.960
Doki!

00:00:47.510 --> 00:00:50.360
I'm gonna tell you a secret.

00:00:50.360 --> 00:00:53.270
Don't tell <i>anyone</i>, okay?

00:00:53.270 --> 00:00:56.160
Even though I'm not girly at all,

00:00:56.160 --> 00:00:58.930
two certain boys said they like me!

00:00:58.930 --> 00:01:01.870
Jump up a bit into the sky.

00:01:01.870 --> 00:01:04.750
My dearest friends are always there.

00:01:04.750 --> 00:01:07.580
Even if you suddenly Character Change,

00:01:07.580 --> 00:01:10.490
I'll be there to stop you with my great big heart.

00:01:10.490 --> 00:01:13.360
Pinky swear!

00:01:13.360 --> 00:01:15.760
Cross my heart!

00:01:16.240 --> 00:01:18.970
Lucky, happy, leave it to me!

00:01:18.970 --> 00:01:22.020
That'd be universal peace, but...

00:01:22.020 --> 00:01:24.770
I'll end up protectin' everyone's hearts.

00:01:24.770 --> 00:01:27.540
Let's all smile together!

00:01:27.540 --> 00:01:30.400
Lucky, happy, leave it to me!

00:01:30.400 --> 00:01:33.210
That's world peace! Yeah, that!

00:01:33.510 --> 00:01:36.440
Everyone has dreams, so I'm gonna protect 'em!

00:01:36.440 --> 00:01:39.260
Make a victory sign together!

00:01:56.080 --> 00:01:58.610
What is the meaning of this?

00:01:58.610 --> 00:02:04.140
As I've said, you are no longer 
affiliated with this company.

00:02:04.140 --> 00:02:05.620
I cannot allow you inside.

00:02:05.620 --> 00:02:08.030
So, what, you don't need me anymore?

00:02:08.030 --> 00:02:11.820
You're using Ikuto to search for the 
Embryo instead, so our business is finished?

00:02:14.090 --> 00:02:16.130
If that's true, so be it.

00:02:29.960 --> 00:02:33.930
Hey... How long am I going to 
be locked up in here?

00:02:35.720 --> 00:02:36.260
Hey.

00:02:37.350 --> 00:02:40.260
I am not allowed to speak to you.

00:02:43.670 --> 00:02:45.260
Sorry.

00:02:48.710 --> 00:02:51.740
They've really upped security since that day.

00:02:59.320 --> 00:03:04.240
Episode 84
Nikaidou-sensei is Actually a Teacher!?

00:03:07.440 --> 00:03:12.020
All right class, your next task is to write an essay about your dreams for the future!

00:03:12.020 --> 00:03:15.730
Sensei, didn't we already do 
that back in first grade?

00:03:15.730 --> 00:03:20.410
It's been a long time since then. I bet many of 
you have changed your minds.

00:03:20.410 --> 00:03:21.500
So please.

00:03:21.500 --> 00:03:23.560
Amu-chan, what will you write?

00:03:23.560 --> 00:03:25.250
What do you want to be?

00:03:25.250 --> 00:03:28.920
I don't know... I haven't decided anything yet...

00:03:32.770 --> 00:03:35.780
For those who don't know or haven't decided,

00:03:35.780 --> 00:03:40.090
you can write something less specific, 
even what you think might be nice.

00:03:41.140 --> 00:03:45.520
Oh, and I won't be showing these to anyone; 
they're for my eyes only.

00:03:45.520 --> 00:03:50.160
Whatever you write will be a 
secret between you-and-me.

00:03:56.920 --> 00:03:58.720
What are you going to write?

00:03:58.720 --> 00:04:01.110
You want to be an artist, right?

00:04:01.110 --> 00:04:03.500
No way, she wants to be a sports star!

00:04:03.500 --> 00:04:05.710
No, a cooking instructor!

00:04:05.710 --> 00:04:08.540
Look here, this isn't about <i>your</i> dreams.

00:04:08.540 --> 00:04:10.390
But they're your dreams, too, Amu-chan.

00:04:10.390 --> 00:04:15.490
Because we were all born from your heart's egg.

00:04:15.490 --> 00:04:18.910
That means our dreams are yours!

00:04:18.910 --> 00:04:19.900
She's got you there!

00:04:20.200 --> 00:04:21.700
Right...

00:04:22.300 --> 00:04:26.000
But I still don't know 
what I actually want to be...

00:04:26.000 --> 00:04:28.680
I just can't decide.

00:04:31.020 --> 00:04:32.580
What you want to be when you grow up, huh?

00:04:32.860 --> 00:04:34.630
I wanna be a baby!

00:04:34.630 --> 00:04:38.840
You can't be a baby when 
you grow up, that's contradictory. {editor: I'm taking advantage of my non-literal translation to rewrite this joke. It's funnier now that the oriignal Japanese which meant something like "being a baby isn't something you want to become, it's something you want to remain"}

00:04:38.840 --> 00:04:41.190
So what about you, Nagihiko?

00:04:42.610 --> 00:04:44.930
What I want to be?

00:04:46.230 --> 00:04:49.200
My second egg still hasn't hatched...

00:04:49.200 --> 00:04:54.080
Inside of it is someone I want to be, 
someone I don't yet know myself.

00:04:57.440 --> 00:05:00.690
I think I'd like to treasure 
this time when my dreams are still dreams. {lit: Perhaps now I want to treasure this time of dreaming}

00:05:00.990 --> 00:05:03.280
That's deep...

00:05:03.280 --> 00:05:04.340
But I get it!

00:05:04.340 --> 00:05:05.670
You do?

00:05:06.880 --> 00:05:09.170
What did you write, Mashiro-san?

00:05:09.170 --> 00:05:10.290
Not telling.

00:05:10.290 --> 00:05:11.840
A comedian! {or if political correctness isn't your style, "comedian!"}

00:05:11.840 --> 00:05:14.080
I did not write that!

00:05:15.060 --> 00:05:17.660
Your dream is to be King of the world, right, Tadase?

00:05:17.660 --> 00:05:19.380
Yeah, and...

00:05:21.670 --> 00:05:25.360
Oh yeah? In the <i>mood</i> 
again today, are we?

00:05:25.360 --> 00:05:27.030
N-No!

00:05:27.470 --> 00:05:30.800
W-Well, maybe, sort of...

00:05:31.400 --> 00:05:35.980
I just hope to make everyone 
happy, including Amu-chan.

00:05:37.170 --> 00:05:38.480
Even Ikuto.

00:05:44.560 --> 00:05:47.810
My Dream - By Hinamori Amu.

00:05:47.810 --> 00:05:53.480
"My mother and father are always saying that children's lives hold infinite possibilities,

00:05:53.480 --> 00:05:56.960
and that we should cherish every one of them."

00:05:56.960 --> 00:06:05.510
"That's why I don't think I can chose only one 
and turn away from all of the others."

00:06:05.710 --> 00:06:08.060
That's so you, Hinamori-san.

00:06:08.060 --> 00:06:09.740
Sensei!

00:06:18.390 --> 00:06:20.460
Oh, Sensei...

00:06:20.460 --> 00:06:21.400
Here.

00:06:21.400 --> 00:06:22.890
Thanks.

00:06:22.890 --> 00:06:25.640
Now, don't get lost on your way home!

00:06:25.640 --> 00:06:27.670
And don't trip anymore!

00:06:29.250 --> 00:06:32.980
Sheesh, he's always been such a klutz.

00:06:32.980 --> 00:06:36.640
Hey, those were our essays, weren't they?

00:06:36.640 --> 00:06:39.240
Yeah. What did you write, Manami?

00:06:39.240 --> 00:06:43.650
You mean about my dream? I want to 
run a flower shop, of course!

00:06:43.650 --> 00:06:44.670
And you, Amu-chan?

00:06:44.970 --> 00:06:46.770
M-Me?

00:06:46.770 --> 00:06:48.330
I...

00:06:48.740 --> 00:06:51.760
I think I'd like to treasure 
this time when my dreams are still dreams.

00:06:52.060 --> 00:06:53.760
So cool!

00:06:54.060 --> 00:06:55.290
Amu-chan...

00:06:55.290 --> 00:06:56.570
That's plagiarism. {editor: alternate, "She's cribbing." but I'm not sure the slang is widespread or appropriate}

00:06:56.570 --> 00:06:58.110
Some heroine...

00:06:58.110 --> 00:07:00.850
Wh-What did you write, Wakana-chan?

00:07:00.850 --> 00:07:04.010
Haven't you always wanted to be a teacher?

00:07:04.010 --> 00:07:04.690
Really?

00:07:05.000 --> 00:07:08.250
Teachers are kind to children, right?

00:07:08.250 --> 00:07:12.670
They lend a helping hand when you have problems or when you're struggling,

00:07:12.670 --> 00:07:17.080
they praise you when you do something good, and scold you when you do bad things.

00:07:17.380 --> 00:07:21.400
And they teach you that learning is fun!

00:07:21.400 --> 00:07:25.960
So I want to be a teacher, 
one like Nikaidou-sensei!

00:07:30.560 --> 00:07:32.400
But all he does is fall all over himself.

00:07:32.400 --> 00:07:34.560
And he has terrible coordination.

00:07:34.560 --> 00:07:36.020
And his fashion sense...

00:07:36.020 --> 00:07:37.100
Doesn't exist.

00:07:37.450 --> 00:07:39.270
His desk is so messy...

00:07:39.270 --> 00:07:41.940
But that's all the more opportunity to clean!

00:07:42.240 --> 00:07:44.030
Don't you think he's unreliable?

00:07:44.030 --> 00:07:44.890
Yeah...

00:07:44.890 --> 00:07:48.290
Can't you tell? Look carefully; 
he's doing a good job.

00:07:48.290 --> 00:07:52.290
He watches over kids who need to study after school,

00:07:52.290 --> 00:07:56.200
and if they're ever sad, he cheers them up.

00:07:57.040 --> 00:07:59.010
Oh, he does?

00:07:59.010 --> 00:08:00.040
That's surprising...

00:08:00.330 --> 00:08:04.620
I'm glad there's at least one kid out 
there who understands him.

00:08:11.140 --> 00:08:12.870
It's from Tadase-kun.

00:08:12.870 --> 00:08:18.400
I still don't know Tsukiyomi Ikuto's 
whereabouts. Has Yoru found any clues?

00:08:18.900 --> 00:08:21.140
Clues, huh?

00:08:24.910 --> 00:08:27.380
Sure doesn't look like he has.

00:08:27.380 --> 00:08:30.090
He's probably tired from searching all day.

00:08:31.250 --> 00:08:34.830
It's better to sleep inside 
your own egg, you know.

00:08:35.800 --> 00:08:37.730
It is-nya?

00:08:38.520 --> 00:08:39.880
Okay...

00:08:39.880 --> 00:08:43.300
That's my egg, not yours!

00:08:43.300 --> 00:08:45.340
You don't have to be so picky-nya...

00:08:45.340 --> 00:08:47.330
I'm not being picky!

00:08:47.950 --> 00:08:49.260
Fine.

00:08:54.040 --> 00:08:56.800
Can't relax around this guy for a second, can we?

00:08:59.220 --> 00:09:02.560
I've never seen anyone talk in their sleep.

00:09:02.910 --> 00:09:04.870
For real?

00:09:04.870 --> 00:09:07.980
But we didn't mean those dreams, we want to 
know your hopes for the future!

00:09:08.280 --> 00:09:10.160
Oh, those!

00:09:10.160 --> 00:09:13.870
Dreams become short-lived the moment you speak them aloud.

00:09:13.870 --> 00:09:17.450
When you write the character for "dream" with the radical for "human," you make the kanji for "fleeting," right?

00:09:18.810 --> 00:09:20.250
Très bien!

00:09:20.250 --> 00:09:22.270
You're splendid, darling!

00:09:22.270 --> 00:09:25.310
I wonder if I couldn't have put 
a better twist on it... {editor: this is an odd phrase, sort of means like, she wishes she could have been a bit wittier in her response. it's literally "a bit more twisted return"}

00:09:25.310 --> 00:09:27.710
That response is so overused. {similar to last line, she's using an expression to mean "the clever response is already pretty common and has been used a lot so is getting old" lit: that response is soiled alread}

00:09:28.060 --> 00:09:30.410
What's your dream, Lulu?

00:09:31.280 --> 00:09:34.470
Won't it disappear if I tell you?

00:09:34.470 --> 00:09:38.890
You know, when you were little, you 
couldn't stop talking about them.

00:09:38.890 --> 00:09:40.960
Every day was so fun.

00:09:40.960 --> 00:09:42.540
You wanted to be a bird for a while.

00:09:42.540 --> 00:09:47.480
Once, you even put wings on and tried to jump out of our apartment in Paris! {note, he says "apartman" which I presume is an abbreviation for "apartment mansion"... unless this is a french term, and I don't think it is, just saying "apartment" is best here}

00:09:47.480 --> 00:09:51.690
And you would always dunk yourself in the bathtub, saying you wanted to be a fish!

00:09:51.990 --> 00:09:53.800
I remember that!

00:09:59.930 --> 00:10:02.310
Gettin' riled up?

00:10:02.310 --> 00:10:03.400
No.

00:10:03.400 --> 00:10:05.290
I actually feel somewhat refreshed.

00:10:05.290 --> 00:10:08.920
It's not like I had any intention of 
giving it to Easter in the first place.

00:10:08.920 --> 00:10:12.910
Not that. I was talking about 
what your mama-san said.

00:10:14.140 --> 00:10:19.630
So? What <i>will</i> you wish 
for if you get the Embryo?

00:10:32.740 --> 00:10:34.600
He is, huh?

00:10:34.600 --> 00:10:36.100
Surprising, isn't it?

00:10:36.510 --> 00:10:38.780
Yeah, but I think I can see it. {note: the original japanese is a double negative "It's not that I can't understand that."

00:10:39.890 --> 00:10:42.570
You've really changed, Mashiro-san.

00:10:44.120 --> 00:10:46.450
Maybe he's been watching over us...

00:10:48.170 --> 00:10:50.370
You think so, Rima?

00:10:50.370 --> 00:10:52.370
Sixth Grade Star Class

00:10:52.750 --> 00:10:55.630
Lose not to the rain, nor the wind,

00:10:55.850 --> 00:10:58.720
nor the snow, nor the heat of summer.

00:10:58.720 --> 00:11:00.680
Nuture thy health...

00:11:05.280 --> 00:11:08.140
Be not greedy; keep thy anger in check...

00:11:11.160 --> 00:11:13.610
Wear always a gentle smile.

00:11:13.610 --> 00:11:18.110
Each day, eat four go of brown rice, 
miso soup, and a portion of vegetables. {editor, "go" is an old fashioned unit of volume equal to .18 liters... considering this is traditional japanese, converting to cups or something seems inappropriate}

00:11:18.410 --> 00:11:20.030
All of these...

00:11:21.410 --> 00:11:22.820
Sensei!

00:11:24.140 --> 00:11:27.020
I don't understand some 
things from that last part.

00:11:27.020 --> 00:11:28.250
Where? Show me.

00:11:28.250 --> 00:11:30.160
Ah, here? This is...

00:11:30.980 --> 00:11:32.850
What is it, Amu-chan?

00:11:32.850 --> 00:11:35.880
Looks like you were right, Wakana-chan!

00:11:36.350 --> 00:11:39.640
Nikaidou-sensei really <i>is</i> a good teacher.

00:11:39.640 --> 00:11:41.900
Yeah, I see it now!

00:11:41.900 --> 00:11:46.460
And you want to be a teacher 
just like him, right?

00:11:47.240 --> 00:11:48.430
No...

00:12:03.780 --> 00:12:05.870
Then what did you mean?

00:12:05.870 --> 00:12:09.890
Didn't you say yesterday that you want 
to be a teacher just like Nikaidou-sensei?

00:12:09.890 --> 00:12:13.890
It's not that I don't want to be like him...

00:12:13.890 --> 00:12:15.960
I just don't know if being 
a teacher is for me.

00:12:16.980 --> 00:12:18.630
What happened?

00:12:18.630 --> 00:12:20.460
Did she have a change of heart?

00:12:21.070 --> 00:12:25.220
I watched a special called "Monster Parents" on TV yesterday. {Aha! TV kills children's dreams. I knew it.}

00:12:25.560 --> 00:12:27.630
Monster Parents?

00:12:27.630 --> 00:12:31.060
It's about parents who 
complain like monsters. {note: Miki is translating the english for amu, basically}

00:12:31.060 --> 00:12:32.640
Monsters?!

00:12:32.640 --> 00:12:38.080
You know, those people who come to school 
and make lots of unreasonable demands. {this is such a japanese phenomena, I wonder if this section will make any sense to people? It's not so easy to explain the incredible power that parents have over schools and teachers in Japan. In many schools, the PTA is the true governing body with the principal and rest of the school staff doing whatever the PTA decides, including curphew and uniform decisions, etc etc...}

00:12:38.080 --> 00:12:41.170
There are a lot of absolutely 
awful parents out there.

00:12:41.170 --> 00:12:43.320
Our daughter was injured!

00:12:43.720 --> 00:12:46.760
That's why I told you 
to hurt that girl right back! {Something is messed up here. The dialogue is in the sign font.}

00:12:47.830 --> 00:12:54.920
As I said, you must sign this 
agreement to raise her grades by 20%.

00:12:56.340 --> 00:13:00.890
I saw them ask a lot of other 
difficult questions on that show!

00:13:00.890 --> 00:13:02.140
I see...

00:13:02.140 --> 00:13:05.710
After I saw that, I started wondering 
if being a teacher is what I really want.

00:13:05.710 --> 00:13:09.360
But hasn't it always been your dream?

00:13:09.360 --> 00:13:11.440
Guess my confidence was shaken...

00:13:11.440 --> 00:13:15.020
Besides, I'm interested 
in tons of other things!

00:13:15.020 --> 00:13:17.910
Like being a stylist or a fashion designer!

00:13:17.910 --> 00:13:22.640
Well, I can totally understand that. {do you remember episode, uh... 55 I think? That was Manami's ? egg episode where she had too many things she wanted to be and got ?'ed... I doubt many people remember it by now}

00:13:22.640 --> 00:13:27.990
We still have plenty of time. It's like an eternity 
before we'll start working, you know?

00:13:28.290 --> 00:13:30.370
That's all I meant.

00:13:30.370 --> 00:13:31.470
See you later.

00:13:39.910 --> 00:13:41.950
I found a lost child.

00:13:41.950 --> 00:13:45.340
What're you doing at someone else's school?

00:13:45.340 --> 00:13:51.120
And why're y'all always targetin' 
Hinamori Amu's friends?

00:13:51.830 --> 00:13:55.230
It's a coincidence! A fluke! 
Mere chance! An accident!

00:13:55.230 --> 00:13:57.580
Face the facts, girl...

00:13:58.470 --> 00:14:00.390
Whaddya think yer doin?!

00:14:00.800 --> 00:14:02.430
Let's go.

00:14:02.430 --> 00:14:04.200
Wait!

00:14:05.230 --> 00:14:06.990
Lulu...

00:14:10.100 --> 00:14:11.780
It's the teacher!

00:14:11.780 --> 00:14:13.540
Hi, Mashiro-san.

00:14:13.540 --> 00:14:15.450
Going to a Guardians' meeting? {hey, isn't it their job to water the flowers? Stop takin' their job, nikaidou!}

00:14:15.450 --> 00:14:18.390
I read your essay.

00:14:18.390 --> 00:14:19.710
Was it weird?

00:14:21.420 --> 00:14:24.760
How dare you laugh at Rima's dream!

00:14:24.760 --> 00:14:28.680
Sorry, your question sort 
of surprised me, is all.

00:14:28.680 --> 00:14:31.520
Who would ever consider your dream weird?

00:14:31.520 --> 00:14:32.740
But...

00:14:32.740 --> 00:14:36.620
Wanting to make people laugh 
is a wonderful thing.

00:14:37.930 --> 00:14:44.190
I'm grateful that you trusted 
me enough to write honestly.

00:14:46.340 --> 00:14:51.670
Hey, Mashiro-san, do you know what kind of flowers will bloom from these sprouts?

00:14:51.670 --> 00:14:52.920
No, what?

00:14:52.920 --> 00:14:54.260
I don't know either.

00:14:54.260 --> 00:14:56.360
He didn't know?! {this is one of those standard tsukkomi responses, but in the middle of this serious scene it's kind of hard to get that across in english. there's a verbal clue in the Japanese, the usage of "-kai" instead of "-ka" for the question marker... that's the main reason I added the ?! instead of just ?. }

00:14:56.360 --> 00:14:59.230
In fact, these sprouts might 
not know, themselves.

00:14:59.230 --> 00:15:03.170
But even so, one day they'll 
bloom into beautiful flowers.

00:15:03.170 --> 00:15:06.320
Dreams are the same...

00:15:07.770 --> 00:15:11.400
And all teachers can do is water them.

00:15:12.100 --> 00:15:16.520
I broke my own heart's egg.

00:15:16.830 --> 00:15:19.130
I'm gonna break you, too!

00:15:20.050 --> 00:15:21.530
My egg...

00:15:22.400 --> 00:15:26.930
I want to make sure that doesn't 
happen to other children.

00:15:26.930 --> 00:15:29.570
It's the least I can do, you know?

00:15:34.950 --> 00:15:36.860
A teacher, huh?

00:15:39.270 --> 00:15:41.670
You're lost, aren't you?

00:15:44.460 --> 00:15:47.280
I'll lend you my power. {what? you're not going to say your catch phrase this week?}

00:15:55.220 --> 00:15:56.390
Rima!

00:15:56.390 --> 00:15:57.310
A ? Egg?

00:15:57.310 --> 00:15:57.640
Yeah!

00:15:58.500 --> 00:15:59.760
A ? Egg?

00:16:00.250 --> 00:16:01.790
Mashiro-san!

00:16:06.920 --> 00:16:09.570
You, read page 34!

00:16:12.260 --> 00:16:15.990
Biff! Kaboom!
I won't lose! I won't lose, dammit!

00:16:16.290 --> 00:16:19.240
Excellent, that will do. 
I'll give you a flower stamp!

00:16:20.350 --> 00:16:21.740
Ow!

00:16:23.210 --> 00:16:26.220
It'll be okay, you can stand!

00:16:26.220 --> 00:16:30.020
Pick yourself up and plant 
those feet on the ground!

00:16:33.470 --> 00:16:35.130
See? You did it!

00:16:35.130 --> 00:16:36.370
Sensei!

00:16:36.370 --> 00:16:38.260
Now, do 200 push-ups!

00:16:44.220 --> 00:16:45.500
Rima!

00:16:45.500 --> 00:16:46.590
Over this way!

00:16:46.590 --> 00:16:47.540
Right!

00:16:47.540 --> 00:16:49.030
Attention!

00:16:50.140 --> 00:16:51.740
Wakana-chan!

00:16:51.740 --> 00:16:53.560
Amu-chan, Mashiro-san!

00:16:53.560 --> 00:16:55.960
I've become a teacher!

00:16:55.960 --> 00:16:58.030
Aren't you just being controlled by a ? Egg?

00:16:59.130 --> 00:17:03.000
I am not! This is who I want to be.

00:17:03.000 --> 00:17:06.010
You of all people should understand!

00:17:16.650 --> 00:17:19.460
Character Transformation: Teacher Dream!

00:17:19.930 --> 00:17:21.990
I'm a teacher!

00:17:24.310 --> 00:17:25.940
Wakana-chan!

00:17:33.060 --> 00:17:36.070
Unkempt clothes lead to unkempt minds! {this is a reference to a standard concept in the 1980s Japanese education systems... one of those political buzzwords, sort of}

00:17:39.990 --> 00:17:44.580
Run wilder and wilder 
and lure out that Embryo!

00:17:46.680 --> 00:17:49.000
What are your dreams for the future?

00:17:49.000 --> 00:17:50.170
Um...

00:17:50.470 --> 00:17:52.980
Now, we can't have you dreamless!

00:17:52.980 --> 00:17:57.350
Only you can make your dreams 
come true, no one can do it for you.

00:17:57.350 --> 00:17:59.160
Bull's eye.

00:17:59.160 --> 00:18:01.210
I know that, sheesh!

00:18:01.210 --> 00:18:03.000
You've gotta grab hold of your dreams yourself!

00:18:03.000 --> 00:18:04.270
Correct!

00:18:06.030 --> 00:18:07.350
Lulu?

00:18:09.070 --> 00:18:11.530
Fall in line!

00:18:12.100 --> 00:18:13.470
You're uneven.

00:18:13.470 --> 00:18:14.720
Let's start over again.

00:18:14.720 --> 00:18:15.700
Rima!

00:18:15.700 --> 00:18:16.700
Right!

00:18:18.490 --> 00:18:21.740
My heart:

00:18:22.090 --> 00:18:23.410
Unlock!

00:18:43.260 --> 00:18:45.470
Character Transformation: Clown Drop!

00:18:47.050 --> 00:18:49.780
Character Transformation: Amulet Spade!

00:18:52.170 --> 00:18:54.700
Wakana-chan, please stop!

00:18:54.700 --> 00:18:57.660
How dare you take that tone with a teacher!

00:18:57.660 --> 00:18:58.820
Attention!

00:19:02.280 --> 00:19:03.790
Right face! {this is the standard marching order phrase, so "right face" is correct while "face right" is not}

00:19:05.390 --> 00:19:07.400
Fall in line, closely!

00:19:07.800 --> 00:19:09.750
Fall in line, spaced apart!

00:19:10.000 --> 00:19:11.780
I can't stop myself!

00:19:11.780 --> 00:19:14.810
I'm the only one who's been 
like this the whole time! {note: because she's in the front of the line. A pretty obtuse joke, I'd say}

00:19:14.810 --> 00:19:16.490
Good, very good.

00:19:16.490 --> 00:19:18.230
Amu!

00:19:19.110 --> 00:19:22.180
That's enough orders out of you! {lit: Argh! It's all orders!}

00:19:25.450 --> 00:19:27.470
Colorful Canvas!

00:19:33.170 --> 00:19:36.060
Juggling Party!

00:19:42.570 --> 00:19:45.910
Aren't teachers supposed to be nice to kids?

00:19:45.910 --> 00:19:48.540
They lend a helping hand when 
they have problems, right?

00:19:48.860 --> 00:19:53.290
And didn't you say they help 
teach kids that learning is fun?

00:19:53.290 --> 00:19:57.210
What would Nikaidou-sensei say 
if he saw you right now?

00:19:58.550 --> 00:20:03.110
No... Have I... made a mistake?

00:20:08.040 --> 00:20:10.640
Negative Heart: Lock on!

00:20:14.270 --> 00:20:16.900
Open Heart!

00:20:47.300 --> 00:20:50.070
Huh? Why are you two here?

00:20:50.720 --> 00:20:52.560
Hey!

00:20:56.070 --> 00:20:58.490
I finally caught up... {man, he is slow. he ran after rima immediately, and yet arrives here 5 or so minutes after the battle started. How big is the damn school grounds? Okay, now I'm just being picky :) }

00:20:58.490 --> 00:21:00.030
Where's the ? Egg?

00:21:03.190 --> 00:21:08.680
Sensei, perfect timing! 
I'm starting to have doubts, you see,

00:21:08.680 --> 00:21:11.000
about what I want to be.

00:21:12.490 --> 00:21:17.960
I thought I'd like to be a teacher, but maybe 
a stylist, or even a fashion designer!

00:21:19.630 --> 00:21:22.070
What's wrong with that?

00:21:22.830 --> 00:21:25.270
Look at all those flowers.

00:21:25.850 --> 00:21:28.240
There are many different types...

00:21:28.240 --> 00:21:30.260
and just as many colors.

00:21:31.100 --> 00:21:35.690
And just like them, people can 
blossom into many different things.

00:21:37.690 --> 00:21:44.030
Ouch, to the point, ain't he? "People can blossom into 
many different things?" Really... {lit: "he stuck you where it hurts"}

00:21:44.340 --> 00:21:46.220
Hey, Lulu!

00:21:47.740 --> 00:21:49.590
Different kinds of flowers.

00:21:49.590 --> 00:21:51.360
Different colors.

00:21:51.360 --> 00:21:52.700
Different smells.

00:21:53.580 --> 00:21:58.250
I wonder if we can make different 
kinds of flowers bloom?

00:21:58.250 --> 00:22:02.000
Of course you can. 
We all have that potential.

00:22:02.260 --> 00:22:06.050
I guess you really are 
a teacher, Nikaidou-sensei.

00:22:06.350 --> 00:22:08.050
You guess?

00:22:08.050 --> 00:22:09.510
What's that supposed to mean?

00:22:09.810 --> 00:22:11.150
She's complimenting you.

00:22:11.150 --> 00:22:12.190
Kind of.

00:22:12.190 --> 00:22:13.550
Right. Kind of.

00:22:13.550 --> 00:22:15.130
Kind of?

00:22:31.840 --> 00:22:36.410
Maybe I was wrong to pretend not to notice your worries.

00:22:36.410 --> 00:22:41.220
It's okay if you can't tell me everything.

00:22:41.220 --> 00:22:43.600
With that dark look on your face,

00:22:43.600 --> 00:22:45.840
go ahead and scream dark things.

00:22:45.840 --> 00:22:50.150
You shouldn't leave all those heavy feelings inside.

00:22:50.150 --> 00:22:51.630
Ride On!

00:22:55.020 --> 00:22:57.830
If you don't... If it's like that...

00:22:57.830 --> 00:23:00.750
You couldn't tell me if you wanted to, huh?

00:23:02.010 --> 00:23:04.500
I get it.

00:23:04.500 --> 00:23:07.160
I'm sure your circumstances will change one day.

00:23:07.160 --> 00:23:10.190
That time will come! That time is now!

00:23:14.010 --> 00:23:15.820
Don't you want to have someone

00:23:15.820 --> 00:23:18.450
say congratulations to you once in your life?

00:23:18.450 --> 00:23:23.380
Doesn't the breeze feel nice today?

00:23:23.380 --> 00:23:27.750
Even if you feel like it's all you can do to survive...

00:23:27.750 --> 00:23:32.620
You can make your life into something you enjoy. It's so nice!

00:23:32.620 --> 00:23:37.440
"Everything's for you."

00:23:37.440 --> 00:23:42.040
How about that?

00:23:43.740 --> 00:23:45.190
My boy!

00:23:50.240 --> 00:23:54.410
Amu-chan, guess what? A glamor model will visit us next time! {A glamor model is an actual type of model and glamor/charisma are synonymous}

00:23:54.410 --> 00:23:55.750
A glamor model?

00:23:55.750 --> 00:23:58.900
Right! Tween glamor model, Sakurai Yua!

00:23:58.900 --> 00:24:00.710
This sure sounds fun!

00:24:00.710 --> 00:24:01.910
You bet it does.

00:24:01.910 --> 00:24:03.000
And who are you?

00:24:03.000 --> 00:24:05.350
I'm Yua-chan's Guardian Character, Cecil!

00:24:05.350 --> 00:24:06.580
Yua has a Guardian Character?

00:24:06.580 --> 00:24:08.520
But why aren't you together?

00:24:08.520 --> 00:24:09.950
Well, about that...

00:24:09.950 --> 00:24:12.170
Next time on Shugo Chara!! Doki!:

00:24:12.170 --> 00:24:14.370
Wassup! Here Comes the Gal Everyone's Talking About!!

00:24:14.370 --> 00:24:17.140
Okay, everyone, all together now:

00:24:17.140 --> 00:24:18.900
Wassup! {well since she's a model and has her picture taken, "Cheese" might be more appropriate. Feel free to change it back if you disagree though. - Asa note, the "usual" translation of "chi-su" is "yo!" but I here something more modernly "cool" sounding is sort of more approprite, since it is really trying (too hard, perhaps) to be cool. Wassup! might be too much, though... cracks me up however :) }
